# Story page: end
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = The Circle Closes
---
Ten relics, ten places, one exhausted snake, and one narrator who has, frankly, seen enough.

{name} laid them in a ring: the brick, the pebble, the stick, the shard, the map, the ember, the core, the scale, the tail tip and the blank page.

The ring glowed. The garden hummed. Far away an old tortoise said 'Finally,' and went back to his rock.

{name} turned, found its own tail waiting, and took one small and legendary bite. It tasted of apples. Of course it did.

And the coil began again, as coils do. I would write 'The End,' but you would not believe me, and I would not blame you.
